--- !u!114 &550316156574744363
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7597653908599029568}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b5bd5e60e42c9624b876a36ed587e020, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  infoTodisplay: The Great Egret (Ardea alba) is a striking wading bird in the heron
    family that graces the Everglades with both elegance and ecological importance.
    Sometimes thought to be merely a color morph of other herons, scientific research
    confirms that the Great Egret is a distinct species, renowned for its unique
    traits and behaviors. As a key indicator of wetland health, this species plays
    a crucial role in maintaining the balance of the ecosystem by preying on small
    fish, amphibians, and invertebrates, thereby regulating their populations. Notable
    for its long, slender legs and sharp, pointed bill, the Great Egret typically
    stands around 3 to 4 feet tall and boasts an impressive wingspan reaching 5 to
    6 feet. Its precise, measured movements through shallow waters and swift strikes
    at unsuspecting prey not only highlight its adept hunting skills but also underscore
    the interconnected roles that each species plays in sustaining the rich biodiversity
    of the Everglades.
  textBoxToReveal: {fileID: 5958484926980042575}
  canvasBase: {fileID: 5684008031019912591}
  interactAudio: {fileID: 855648684129327504}
  canvasPopupHeight: 5
